{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1093926-the-iterators-supernal-through-simulations-hombrew-legacy","id":1093926,"title":"The Iterators - Supernal through Simulations (Hombrew Legacy)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-17T18:10:10-07:00","id":1093926,"title":"The Iterators - Supernal through Simulations (Hombrew Legacy)","content":"Hey all. This is another homebrew Legacy I've been cooking up for a little bit now, the &quot;Iterators&quot;.<br /> I originally tried to think of a way to mesh technology into Mystic practice, before coming up with an entirely new concept.<br /> Basically this Legacy is a glorification of &quot;practice makes perfect&quot;, using tools such a modelling, virtual simulations and even simple calculations to enhance the use of spells.<br /> I'm still working on the Attainments, but they're mostly about enhancing Yantras, and reaching the Supernal &quot;source code&quot; for Platonic Forms and &quot;truth&quot; applications.<br /> <br /> <b>Iterators</b><br /> The Supernal Realms, as noted by many are not a physical \u201cplace\u201d, they are a realm of subjectivity and symbolism, pure meaning without the constraints of petty fallen physicality. This concept has long been difficult for Mages to communicate to others, due to the lack of a readily available real-world point of reference. Philosophical theories such as Plato\u2019s theory of the Forms can assist in this understanding, however explaining a purely conceptual theory is difficult for those who have not much experience turning concepts into reality.<br /> The 20<sup>th</sup> Century changed that however, for while mankind progressed in a great many technological field, one specifically caught the eye of many Mages for its applications in Willworking.<br /> Virtual Reality.<br /> <br /> The concept of a simulated reality, defined by code and fully workable by one who could comprehend that Code was a great blessing for the Mysterium. This was at last a powerful metaphor, usable by even the most dim witted Sleepers for the interaction between the Supernal Realms, and the Fallen World. Some Mages went even further than the mere acceptable of this analogy, and turned their attention to internalizing this symbol and using its power to further enhance their Awakened Magic.<br /> This was the birth of the Iterators. Born towards the end of the 20<sup>th</sup> Century, the core concept of the Legacy is that reality is akin to a simulation, in fact, some of the more philosophical amongst their number would say it is impossible to definitively prove that reality is NOT a simulation. Through experimenting with the readily available Fallen concept of simulations, Mages can practice and refine the Imagos they use to cast spells, and empower their \u201creal\u201d spellcasting.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, some have derided this Legacy as being a mere glorification of practice, something which all Mages and even Sleepers must engage in should they wish to enhance their skills. Despite this, it cannot be denied that the Iterators, through continual improvement and refining of their spells, are more capable than most Mages at casting spells they have dutifully prepared and practiced over, and over, and over again, even without use of a Rote or Praxis. Some see the iterators as more of a Technologically based Legacy, and while every Member is computer savvy, the Legacy ultimately sees technology as a mere tool, a more efficient tool than those used in ages past, but a mere tool nonetheless. An Iterator can make use of most of his Yantras with but pen and paper, after all.<br /> <br /> Doctrine <br /> <b>Parentage: </b>Obrimos, Mysterium<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Prime 2, High Speech, Computers 2 and 2 dots between Crafts, Occult and Investigation<br /> <b>Initiation:</b> Bring before your Mentor a single, specific spell which you have practiced and refined as far as you can bring it in your current state, then cast it with an Exceptional Success. Use of Rotes is forbidden, and Praxes are only permitted if they have been developed, rather than achieved through inspiration (purchased with an Experience, not gained Free through Gnosis). (Not too sure about this one, basically impress your mentor with your devotion to practicing a specific spell).<br /> <br /> <br /> Magic: <br /> <b>Ruling: </b>Prime<br /> <b>Yantras: </b>Succeed on a Computers test relevant to the spell (+2), spend a scene developing, analyzing and \u201cbug testing\u201d your Imago prior to casting (+2), performing a spell you have repeatedly performed beforehand in similar circumstances (+1), casting a Praxis (+1), spend a turn identifying they key aspects of reality that your spell shall manipulate (+1).<br /> <b>Oblations: </b>Develop or brainstorm new methods of manipulating reality (even if unable to personally enact them), study and improve your understanding of High Speech (the language of the Supernal), experiment with simulations of reality or willworking, attend or give a presentation on your developments of an imago.<br /> <br /> Simularities should be obious to various cWoD groups, but I tried to keep the quintessential essence of Awakening in mind through its creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}